.TH ASTERCTL-UNSUBSCRIBE 1 "2026-10-06" "Aster" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
asterctl-unsubscribe \- remove an Event subscription
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY asterctl
.RI [ GLOBAL-OPTIONS ]
.B unsubscribe
.I SUBSCRIPTION_ID
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove one Event subscription using the DeleteEventSubscription RPC.
The required argument is a Base64 ID decoding to exactly 32 bytes, as printed by
.BR asterctl-subscribe (1)
or
.BR asterctl-subscriptions (1).
Invalid arguments are rejected before token-file access or network activity.
.PP
There is no confirmation, stdin input, operation key, or automatic retry.
.SH OPTIONS
Accepts the global options described in
.BR asterctl (1),
before or after the command.
.B \-\-help
requires no token or subscription ID.
.SH OUTPUT
Prints "Subscription removed" or "Subscription already absent", followed by a newline.
Both outcomes are successful.
.PP
With \-\-json, prints a pretty ProtoJSON object containing only the boolean
.B alreadyAbsent
field: false when removed, true when already absent. The false default is included.
.SH RECOVERY
A timeout, lost connection, or malformed response can leave the outcome unknown:
the agent may already have committed the removal. For example:
.PP
.nf
.RS
asterctl: DeleteEventSubscription outcome unknown: deadline_exceeded
retry unsubscribe with the same subscription ID
.RE
.fi
.PP
Retry manually against the same agent with the same ID.
Confirmed rejections report fixed RPC codes, not remote messages or tokens.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Removed, already absent, or help displayed. A closed stdout pipe is also successful.
.TP
.B 1
RPC, authentication, or I/O error, including an unknown mutation outcome.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid or missing arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.RS
asterctl \-\-token\-file ./client.token unsubscribe "$SUBSCRIPTION_ID"
asterctl \-\-token\-file ./client.token unsubscribe "$SUBSCRIPTION_ID" \-\-json
asterctl unsubscribe \-\-help
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asterctl (1),
.BR asterctl-subscribe (1),
.BR asterctl-subscriptions (1)
